---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const description =
  'The rules for using Clipwell: permitted public-media downloads, prohibited access bypasses, user responsibilities, availability limits and liability.';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description={description}
  path="/terms-of-service/"
>
  <p>
    These Terms of Service govern your use of the Clipwell website and downloader API. By using the
    service, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use Clipwell. If you use the
    service for an organisation, you confirm that you have authority to accept these terms for it.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What Clipwell provides</h2>

  <p>
    Clipwell is a technical utility that reads public media pages and downloads the video, audio or
    caption tracks those pages expose. It supports a limited set of platforms and only operates on
    public URLs. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by any supported platform.
  </p>

  <p>
    The service is provided on an “as available” basis. Features, supported platforms, format
    availability and limits may change as the underlying sources and infrastructure change.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Eligibility</h2>

  <p>
    You must be old enough to enter a binding contract in your jurisdiction and at least 13 years old.
    If you are under the age of majority where you live, use Clipwell only with the involvement of a
    parent or guardian. Do not use the service if you are barred from doing so by applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Permitted use</h2>

  <p>
    You may use Clipwell to download public media that you own, that you have permission to download,
    or that you may lawfully copy under an applicable exception. You may use the site for personal
    research, archiving, accessibility or other lawful purposes, provided your use complies with
    copyright law, platform terms and these terms.
  </p>

  <p>
    Public visibility does not make content freely reusable. A public video can still be protected by
    copyright, trademark, privacy or other rights. You are responsible for determining whether your
    download and any later use are permitted.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Prohibited use</h2>

  <p>You may not use Clipwell to:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>access private, deleted, subscriber-only, age-restricted or login-protected content;</li>
    <li>bypass DRM, encryption, paywalls, authentication, region controls or other access measures;</li>
    <li>infringe copyright, trademark, privacy, publicity or other rights;</li>
    <li>harass, stalk, exploit or harm another person, or publish private information;</li>
    <li>download or distribute sexual content involving minors, malware or illegal material;</li>
    <li>send automated or bulk requests, bypass rate limits, probe the API or interfere with the service;</li>
    <li>resell, sublicense or rebrand the service without written permission;</li>
    <li>misrepresent downloaded media as your own or remove lawful attribution; or</li>
    <li>violate the terms of the platform whose content you are accessing.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    We may block requests, restrict access or refuse service when we believe these rules have been
    broken or when continued processing would create a legal, security or operational risk.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Your responsibilities</h2>

  <p>
    You are responsible for the links you submit and for how you use the resulting files. You must
    not submit credentials, session cookies, private media or links containing sensitive tokens. You
    are also responsible for keeping your own device, accounts and network secure.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you share downloaded material, you are responsible for any required permissions, licences,
    attribution and royalty obligations. Clipwell does not grant any licence to content it downloads.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Intellectual property</h2>

  <p>
    The Clipwell name, interface, design and original site content are protected by the operator’s
    intellectual-property rights. You may not copy the site wholesale or use its branding in a way
    that suggests endorsement. Third-party names, logos and media remain the property of their
    respective owners. Clips and files downloaded through the service are not owned by Clipwell.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Third-party platforms</h2>

  <p>
    The service depends on public pages and data from third-party platforms. Their terms, privacy
    policies and technical behaviour apply to your use of those platforms. Clipwell does not control
    their availability, accuracy, content or access rules, and is not responsible for a platform’s
    decision to remove, restrict or authenticate a post.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Downloads, limits and retention</h2>

  <p>
    Requests may be subject to rate limits, concurrency limits, file-size limits and processing
    timeouts. Downloads can fail because a source is private, restricted, unavailable, too large,
    unsupported or temporarily blocked. Temporary files are deleted automatically after a short
    period. Clipwell is not a storage service; download your file promptly.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Disclaimers</h2>

  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, Clipwell is provided “as is” and “as available”, without
    warranties of any kind, express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose,
    non-infringement, availability, accuracy or uninterrupted operation. Some jurisdictions do not
    allow the exclusion of certain warranties, so parts of this section may not apply to you.
  </p>

  <p>
    The service does not provide legal advice, and checking whether a download is lawful remains your
    responsibility. See the <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> and
    <a href="/copyright-policy/">Copyright Policy</a> for more detail.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2>

  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, the operator and its contributors will not be liable for
    indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, loss of data, loss of profits,
    loss of reputation, copyright claims arising from your use, or any failure caused by a third-party
    platform or network. Where liability cannot be excluded, it is limited to the amount you paid to
    use the service, which is currently zero.
  </p>

  <p>
    Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited, including liability for
    fraud or for death or personal injury caused by negligence where applicable law prohibits such a
    limitation.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Indemnity</h2>

  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, you agree to indemnify and hold harmless the operator from claims,
    losses and reasonable costs arising out of your misuse of the service, your violation of these
    terms, or your infringement of another party’s rights.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Suspension and changes</h2>

  <p>
    We may suspend, change or discontinue all or part of the service at any time, including when a
    platform changes its technology or when operating the service becomes impractical. We may revise
    these terms by updating this page and its date. Continued use after a revision means you accept
    the revised terms.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Governing law</h2>

  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws applicable in the jurisdiction where the operator is
    established, without regard to conflict-of-laws rules. Courts in that jurisdiction will have
    exclusive jurisdiction, except where mandatory consumer law gives you the right to bring a claim
    elsewhere. If any provision is unenforceable, the remaining provisions stay in effect.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Contact</h2>

  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.legalEmail}`}>{SITE.legalEmail}</a>. General
    support: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>. These terms are a
    practical service agreement, not legal advice.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
